+**Stages that need a module before it arrives** (flagged for the owner; the table chooses none of them):
+
+- **grep at 18: command-line input gap.** The adopted `grep PATTERN FILE` stage needs argument access (the [showcase plan](docs/proposals/EXAMPLES.md#showcases)), but args/cli are not placed. The legacy accessor returns an allocating String (`legacy/std/src/args.con` line 22); legacy CLI stores Vec/String (`legacy/std/src/cli.con` line 27, `legacy/std/src/cli.con` line 50). Allocation arrives at 19 and Vec/String at 22 (slice 19 of the [slice table](#vertical-slices), slice 22 of the [slice table](#vertical-slices)), after zero-heap slice 18 (slice 18 of the [slice table](#vertical-slices)). A nonallocating argument contract is unresolved; this table does not choose one. The same gap applies to the file encryptor at 18 if it takes command-line paths, which its adopted row does not specify.
+- **All early byte consumers: legacy Bytes cannot be carried unchanged.** EVM 15, crypto 15/18, grep fixed buffers 16/18, QOI 19/21, PNG 21 and Wasm 21 need byte operations before growable Vec storage at 22; Bytes itself is unplaced. Legacy Bytes owns raw, allocating storage (`legacy/std/src/bytes.con` line 7, `legacy/std/src/bytes.con` line 30); allocation is 19 and source raw pointers are 24 (slice 19 of the [slice table](#vertical-slices), slice 24 of the [slice table](#vertical-slices)). Fixed arrays/views at 15 and HeapArray at 21 support earlier safe implementations; they do not establish a Bytes module placement. The stage rows are the [showcase plan](docs/proposals/EXAMPLES.md#showcases).
+- **EVM 21 growable memory: potential container conflict.** The showcase asks for growable memory in its 21 → 23 expansion (the [showcase plan](docs/proposals/EXAMPLES.md#showcases)), while HeapArray at 21 is fixed-length and Vec arrives at 22 (slice 21 of the [slice table](#vertical-slices), slice 22 of the [slice table](#vertical-slices)). If growth is required at 21, its implementation contract is missing; the row does not establish that Vec arrives early.
+- **Unplaced codec/crypto dependencies.** QOI 19/21, PNG 21–22, EVM 15/21/23 and Wasm 21 need endian byte operations; PNG also needs CRC32, and EVM's full version needs Keccak (the [showcase plan](docs/proposals/EXAMPLES.md#showcases), the [showcase plan](docs/proposals/EXAMPLES.md#showcases), the [showcase plan](docs/proposals/EXAMPLES.md#showcases)). Their module arrivals are not placed, so these are scheduling gaps, not demonstrable later-slice conflicts. DEFLATE is an adopted PNG program requirement, not an independently scheduled std module. The crypto 7 stage is scalar only: arrays arrive at 15, so complete array-based ChaCha20/Poly1305/X25519 implementations cannot be claimed at 7 (slice 7 of the [slice table](#vertical-slices), slice 15 of the [slice table](#vertical-slices); the [showcase plan](docs/proposals/EXAMPLES.md#showcases)).
+- **Proposed base64 at 17: legacy implementation conflicts.** This is not an adopted placement (the [showcase plan](docs/proposals/EXAMPLES.md#showcases), the [showcase plan](docs/proposals/EXAMPLES.md#showcases)). Legacy encode/decode allocate Bytes (`legacy/std/src/base64.con` line 40, `legacy/std/src/base64.con` line 62), before allocation at 19 and growable containers at 22; a fixed-buffer version has no decided API.
+- No other definite stage-before-module conflict follows from the adopted rows: maps arrive with store/EVM/Wasm stage 23; network/time arrive with the sequential server at 27. RocksDB acceptance is **after 25**, and ethlambda **after 28**, both subject to the R-0604 dependency audit (R-0604, R-0285, R-0490); their complete module requirements must not be inferred as already audited. No concurrency model is chosen here.
